2026-09-01 00:54:30.132 | DEBUG    | app.model.gpt:call:247 - BadRequestError (400): messages=[{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a pull request reviewer. You need to choose the one PR from multiple that actually will resolve the given issue.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Here is the issue: <issue>Issue Title: [FEATURE] Dont persist agent state if there were no updates to it\n\nDescription:\n### Problem Statement\n\nAs a user of strands session manager, I would not like to persist changes to session if the agents state was not updated.\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nAdd a flag to agent state to mark that a change has been made. Then session manager can check if this flag is set, and use it to determine if a change should be pushed\n\n### Use Case\n\nReduce the number of `update_agent` calls needed to be made by the session manager\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\nBased on clarification discussion and repository analysis:\n\n### Technical Approach\n\n#### 1. Add Dirty Flag to `JSONSerializableDict`\n**File:** `src/strands/types/json_dict.py`\n\n- Add `_dirty: bool` instance attribute, initialized to `False`\n- Set `_dirty = True` when `set()` is called\n- Set `_dirty = True` when `delete()` is called\n- Add `_is_dirty() -> bool` private method to check dirty status\n- Add `_clear_dirty() -> None` private method to reset flag to `False`\n\n> **Note:** Methods are prefixed with `_` to indicate they are internal implementation details for use by the session manager, not part of the public API.\n\n#### 2. Modify `sync_agent()` in `RepositorySessionManager`\n**File:** `src/strands/session/repository_session_manager.py`\n\n- Track the previously synced `_internal_state` for comparison (diffing)\n- Before calling `update_agent()`, check:\n  - `agent.state._is_dirty()` for user-managed state changes\n  - Direct comparison of current vs. previously synced `_internal_state`\n- Only call `update_agent()` if either condition is true\n- Clear dirty flag only **after successful sync** (keep set on failure for retry)\n- Update tracked `_internal_state` after successful sync\n\n### Scope Boundaries\n\n- ✅ **In Scope:** `sync_agent()` for single `Agent` only\n- ❌ **Out of Scope (future follow-up):**\n  - `sync_multi_agent()` optimization\n  - `sync_bidi_agent()` optimization\n  - Force sync option\n  - `conversation_manager_state` dirty tracking (changes infrequently)\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/strands/types/json_dict.py` | Add `_dirty` flag, `_is_dirty()`, `_clear_dirty()` private methods |\n| `src/strands/session/repository_session_manager.py` | Add dirty check logic in `sync_agent()`, track internal state |\n| `tests/strands/types/test_json_dict.py` | Add unit tests for dirty flag behavior |\n| `tests/strands/session/test_repository_session_manager.py` | Add tests for conditional sync behavior |\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `False` after initialization\n- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `True` after `set()` is called\n- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `True` after `delete()` is called\n- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._clear_dirty()` resets dirty flag to `False`\n- [ ] `sync_agent()` skips `update_agent()` call when state is not dirty and internal state unchanged\n- [ ] `sync_agent()` calls `update_agent()` when `agent.state` is dirty\n- [ ] `sync_agent()` calls `update_agent()` when internal state has changed\n- [ ] Dirty flag remains set if `update_agent()` fails (for retry on next sync)\n- [ ] All existing session manager tests continue to pass\n- [ ] New unit tests cover dirty flag behavior\n\n### Additional Context\n\nThis optimization reduces unnecessary I/O operations (file writes, S3 puts, etc.) when the agent processes messages without modifying its state, improving performance especially in high-throughput scenarios.</issue>.\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'First, please analyze the root cause of the issue.'}]
